The question comes up:  What does it mean when I am "killed by a
system shock"?

Let's check the code...

SPOILER ALERT


When the game attempts to polymorph you (either because of a ring
of polymorph or a polymorph trap), and you do not have polymorph
control (i.e., you're not wearing a ring of polymorph control), a
check is made against your character's constitution.  A random
number between 0 and 19 (inclusive) is generated.  If this is
less than or equal to your constitution, then the polymorph
succeeds.  (Thus, the higher your constitution, the better your
chances of polymorphing successfully.)

If the random number is greater than your constitution, the
polymorph fails.  In this case, you get the message "You shudder
for a moment", you take from 0 to 29 hit points of damage, and
you remain as you are.  If the damage kills you, then your epitaph
will read "Killed by a system shock."  In other words, you died
because your "system" wasn't tough enough to withstand the shock
of being polymorphed.



